msgid "expedition.feedback.missing_input"
msgstr "Hopeless. Something necessary is missing."

msgid "expedition.feedback.light.hopeless"
msgstr "Impossible. Your mind is dark."
msgid "expedition.feedback.light.maybe"
msgstr "Perhaps. A cold light gathers at the edge of thought."
msgid "expedition.feedback.light.enough"
msgstr "Enough. Thought turns clear, and no small doubt can hide."
msgid "expedition.feedback.tear.hopeless"
msgstr "Impossible. Not a ripple moves through your heart."
msgid "expedition.feedback.tear.maybe"
msgstr "Perhaps. A certain sorrow is beginning to gain weight."
msgid "expedition.feedback.tear.enough"
msgstr "Enough. You hear what the silence was trying to say."
msgid "expedition.feedback.dream.hopeless"
msgstr "Impossible. Nothing happens inside the imagining."
msgid "expedition.feedback.dream.maybe"
msgstr "Perhaps. The edge of reality is coming slightly loose."
msgid "expedition.feedback.dream.enough"
msgstr "Enough. The vision is more real than what stands before you."
msgid "expedition.feedback.sleep.hopeless"
msgstr "Impossible. Your body remains taut."
msgid "expedition.feedback.sleep.maybe"
msgstr "Perhaps. Your breathing is finding a steady rhythm."
msgid "expedition.feedback.sleep.enough"
msgstr "Enough. The body remembers how to endure this moment in peace."

msgid "expedition.room.rest.result"
msgstr "You remain here for a while. A neglected part of you grows back by one small degree."
msgid "expedition.room.rest.empty_result"
msgstr "You do not rest. You keep wandering here instead, until you pick up a few silver things. [money+20]"
msgid "expedition.room.rest.no_growth"
msgstr "You find rest. Though the diversion does not become part of you, your body remembers these quiet hours."
msgid "expedition.room.rest.no_growth_healed_wound"
msgstr "You find rest. Though the diversion does not become part of you, at least one of your wounds has healed. [Wound-1]"
msgid "expedition.room.salvage.result"
msgstr "The machine swallows these things and returns money that still works."
msgid "expedition.room.work.result"
msgstr "You keep arranging shelves that have no end. Six hours later, a few silver things remain in your palm. [money+20]"
msgid "expedition.disease.wound.removed_white_flower"
msgstr "As the wound opens across your heart, one white flower withers. [White Flower-1]"

msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.name"
msgstr "Spaceship Book City"
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.intro.1"
msgstr "Marble steps climb toward a row of astronauts hanging without helmets."
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.intro.2"
msgstr "They kneel around an open book. With no wind, its pages keep returning to the same place."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.name"
msgstr "Gray Hall"
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.intro.1"
msgstr "Gray Hall has no shadows. Tiles, wallpaper, and chandeliers share one faded color."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.intro.2"
msgstr "At its center, a cassette-headed woman plays the piano. The melody is correct almost to the point of cruelty."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.name"
msgstr "Birthday Party"
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.intro.1"
msgstr "A false fireplace lights an aging Western restaurant. Balloons, banners, and streamers wait for the party to end."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.intro.2"
msgstr "Birthday candles burn on the table, but every chair is empty."

msgid "expedition.room.retro_restaurant.name"
msgstr "Retro Restaurant"
msgid "expedition.room.retro_restaurant.intro.1"
msgstr "The red booth still holds the warmth of its previous guests."
msgid "expedition.room.retro_restaurant.intro.2"
msgstr "The menu suggests trading a meal for a brief calm."
msgid "expedition.room.home.name"
msgstr "Home"
msgid "expedition.room.home.intro.1"
msgstr "Behind the door is a home that belongs to no address."
msgid "expedition.room.home.intro.2"
msgstr "You may leave something here and pretend you truly returned."
msgid "expedition.room.rainforest.name"
msgstr "Rainforest"
msgid "expedition.room.rainforest.intro.1"
msgstr "Wet leaves grow through cracks in the mall and cover the ceiling."
msgid "expedition.room.rainforest.intro.2"
msgstr "Let one Persona you already possess enter; the rain will raise it by one."
msgid "expedition.room.salvage_yard.name"
msgstr "Salvage Yard"
msgid "expedition.room.salvage_yard.intro.1"
msgstr "Scales, conveyor belts, and an iron mouth that never closes."
msgid "expedition.room.salvage_yard.intro.2"
msgstr "It asks no provenance. It recognizes only the original price."

msgid "expedition.room.shelf_shift.name"
msgstr "Shelf Shift"
msgid "expedition.room.shelf_shift.intro.1"
msgstr "Tonight's shelves are longer than by day, and hungrier."
msgid "expedition.room.shelf_shift.intro.2"
msgstr "Return the goods to their places. The Rainforest Group will pay twenty."

msgid "expedition.room.scanner.name"
msgstr "The Scanner"
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.intro.1"
msgstr "A conveyor enters the dark beneath a sign that reads: TO THE SECOND FLOOR."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.intro.2"
msgstr "You stand between two boxes. The belt has started moving, and this building has no second floor."
msgid "expedition.reward.salvage.name"
msgstr "Found Object"
msgid "expedition.reward.salvage.description"
msgstr "Something retrieved from a corner of the room. It is still worth eight; perhaps that is its only clear provenance."
msgid "expedition.reward.wound.name"
msgstr "Wound"
msgid "expedition.reward.wound.description"
msgstr "Another wound has opened on my heart. Coagulated concrete flows from it. [At three, the game ends. I need to rest, or think of a way inside the bag.]"
msgid "expedition.reward.wage.name"
msgstr "Wages +20"
msgid "expedition.reward.wage.description"
msgstr "Six hours folded into twenty coins. The Rainforest Group never asks what you saw behind the shelves."

msgid "expedition.disease.white_flower.name"
msgstr "White Flower"
msgid "expedition.disease.white_flower.description"
msgstr "My throat itches. I know flowers are growing there. One day they will pierce my skull and bloom above my head. [At three, the game ends. I need to face the challenge, or think of a way inside the bag.]"
msgid "expedition.property.disease.name"
msgstr "Disease"
msgid "expedition.property.disease.description"
msgstr "A change accumulating inside me. [A Disease can only enter the material slot of the in-bag synthesis table.]"
msgid "expedition.recipe.clear_white_flower.name"
msgstr "Remove White Flower"
msgid "expedition.recipe.clear_white_flower.hint"
msgstr "The flower has not pierced bone yet. Reason can trace its roots; empathy can remember a throat in which it never grew."
msgid "expedition.recipe.base.white_flower"
msgstr "One White Flower"
msgid "expedition.recipe.clear_white_flower.process.1"
msgstr "The roots search the bottom of the bag for a vein that does not exist."
msgid "expedition.recipe.clear_white_flower.process.2"
msgstr "I name its color, or remember my throat without it. The white flower withers."
msgid "expedition.recipe.clear_wound.name"
msgstr "Remove Wound"
msgid "expedition.recipe.clear_wound.hint"
msgstr "The concrete has not fully set. Rest can close the breach; reverie can make it forget its shape."
msgid "expedition.recipe.base.wound"
msgstr "One Wound"
msgid "expedition.recipe.clear_wound.process.1"
msgstr "The wound opens its mouth and coughs up a small gray city."
msgid "expedition.recipe.clear_wound.process.2"
msgstr "I put it to sleep, or let it dream it never split. The concrete stops flowing."
msgid "expedition.ui.disease_end.white_flower"
msgstr "The white flowers finally pierce my skull and bloom above my head.\nTonight's expedition has not begun, but the game is already over."
msgid "expedition.ui.disease_end.expedition_wound"
msgstr "The third wound crosses my heart. Coagulated concrete fills the paper bag.\nTonight's expedition has not begun, but the game is already over."

msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.challenge.1"
msgstr "The foremost astronaut shifts one knee aside, leaving you a patch of cold marble."
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.challenge.2"
msgstr "The altar is never at the center of sight. Each attempt to focus sends it behind another shelf."
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.kneel.title"
msgstr "Kneel Among Them"
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.kneel.prompt"
msgstr "You could join the astronauts and kneel on the marble, using [b]yourself[/b] and your [color=#9a78c5]imagination[/color] to comprehend the thing they worship."
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.kneel.success"
msgstr "Pages press themselves to your forehead. Cities, streets, and citizens that never existed fill your skull. The astronauts rise together and leave the lower volume on your knees."
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.kneel.failure"
msgstr "You kneel as low as they do. The pages turn faster until nothing remains but unwritten white. The astronauts slowly close the gap around you."
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.investigate.title"
msgstr "Investigate the Altar"
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.investigate.prompt"
msgstr "You could treat this place as a case that still has an answer. Use [b]a book[/b] to align the disordered shelves, and let [color=#f2d14f]investigation[/color] reveal where the altar truly stands."
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.investigate.success"
msgstr "Every shelf casts its shadow toward one point. You pull Welcome to Concrete City, Lower Volume out of empty air. The astronauts remain kneeling, as if they never noticed the altar go bare."
msgid "expedition.room.spaceship_library_city.investigate.failure"
msgstr "Every clue denies another. The shelves exchange places at the edge of sight. The altar vanishes one conclusion ahead of you."

msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.challenge.1"
msgstr "She suddenly accelerates. Bar lines tear apart, and the keys make sounds no piano owns."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.challenge.2"
msgstr "No mistakes... not a single wrong note. Her fingers keep running."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.music.title"
msgstr "Play Some Music"
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.music.prompt"
msgstr "Perhaps another sound can make her hear herself. You could [b]play some music[/b], using [color=#f2d14f]lucid thought[/color] to find the note she keeps avoiding inside the noise."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.music.success"
msgstr "The two cassettes synchronize for a moment. She stops inside an unfinished measure. Not her. Not me. Her body fades into gray; only the cassette continues to breathe."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.music.failure"
msgstr "She winds the new melody into her playing and crushes it into sharper noise. She never looks up, but the gray advances one step."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.listen.title"
msgstr "Stay and Listen"
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.listen.prompt"
msgstr "You could sit where she cannot see you and let [b]yourself[/b] keep [color=#6faed9]listening[/color]. Do not correct her. Do not interrupt. Endure everything the music remembers."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.listen.success"
msgstr "The music slows. You heard it? ...She never... played it wrong. The woman vanishes from the bench, leaving one cassette still warm."
msgid "expedition.room.gray_hall.listen.failure"
msgstr "You hear many emotions, but none of them are hers. The music snaps shut and leaves you outside the gray."

msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.challenge.1"
msgstr "A balloon bursts in the next room. One pop. Then another."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.challenge.2"
msgstr "The door opens. A birthday cake enters on a child's body, and every candle turns toward you."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.gift.title"
msgstr "Offer a Gift"
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.gift.prompt"
msgstr "You could give him [b]a toy[/b] or [b]a flower[/b]: something that lets him [color=#6faed9]weep[/color] in the candlelight, yet gives his body [color=#f3c6d6]comfort[/color]."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.gift.success"
msgstr "He embraces the gift. For the first time, the mouth in the icing droops. Tears put out the candles. In the dark, he removes his own head and solemnly gives it to you."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.gift.failure"
msgstr "He holds the gift up to the candles and waits. Wax crosses the tablecloth. His smile never changes. Another balloon bursts next door."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.sing.title"
msgstr "Sing Happy Birthday"
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.sing.prompt"
msgstr "You could place [b]yourself[/b] before the candles, [color=#f3c6d6]relax your body and voice[/color], and finish the song everyone remembers."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.sing.success"
msgstr "He applauds softly when the final note falls. Wish, candles, growing up. The steps are finally over. He removes the cake head and places it in your hands."
msgid "expedition.room.birthday_party.sing.failure"
msgstr "The song sounds alien in a room meant to be warm. He shields the candles until your voice and their flames go out together."

msgid "expedition.room.scanner.round1.challenge.1"
msgstr "Scanner-headed figures stand in a perfect line in the dark. Green beams light one after another."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.round1.challenge.2"
msgstr "The conveyor carries you toward them. Sealed boxes stand before and behind you. You do not know who put them there."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.face.title"
msgstr "Face the Scan"
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.face.prompt"
msgstr "You could place [b]yourself[/b] beneath the green beam and [color=#f2d14f]reason out[/color] an airtight argument that the shopping bag truly is your head."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.face.success"
msgstr "Green light travels from the mouth of the bag to your shoulders. Beep. Pass. Is my head still there? When you lift the bag, your shoulders feel suddenly weightless."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.face.failure"
msgstr "Your argument becomes meaningless before the first beep. The green light repeatedly confirms the outline that should not exist beneath the bag."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.hide.title"
msgstr "Hide Behind a Box"
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.hide.prompt"
msgstr "You could let [b]yourself[/b] hide behind a box and use [color=#9a78c5]imagination[/color] to forget you are moving, forget the scanner beeps, forget all those green gazes."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.hide.success"
msgstr "You forget the conveyor, so the conveyor forgets you. Green light crosses an ordinary box and does not stop."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.hide.failure"
msgstr "The box grows immense inside the imagining, but your real shadow remains exposed. Every green gaze turns toward you."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.round2.challenge.1"
msgstr "The conveyor reaches an atrium too vast for its building, then drops in a straight line from high above."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.round2.challenge.2"
msgstr "A gigantic scanner casts its light upon the cliff. Your turn. There is nowhere to hide. What is in your bag?"
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.time.title"
msgstr "The Corpse of Time"
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.time.prompt"
msgstr "You leave [b]yourself[/b] in the light and let your [color=#f3c6d6]tired body[/color] answer. You say you do not know why you are here. You have no wish to play some retro game. You only want to leave, go home, and sleep."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.time.success"
msgstr "The great scanner falls silent. Then it reads a corpse of time from 2020: tired, real, still wanting to go home. The cliff releases you."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.time.failure"
msgstr "It finds no home. Only an invalid date expiring again and again inside the bag. The conveyor begins to tilt."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.rose.title"
msgstr "The Memory of a Yellow Rose"
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.rose.prompt"
msgstr "You could lift [b]a flower[/b] into the green light. Let it carry the [color=#f3c6d6]warmth of someone asleep[/color] and a [color=#9a78c5]memory that may never have happened[/color], answering with what remains inside the bag."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.rose.success"
msgstr "The scanner reads a market stripped bare, a song that wakes no one, and a yellow rose that never existed. You fall from the cliff and wake underground before a safety exit."
msgid "expedition.room.scanner.rose.failure"
msgstr "The flower loses its color in the green light. Memory and sleep deny each other. The scanner marks you as unclaimed merchandise."

msgid "debug.ui.opening_rules"
msgstr "Opening"

msgid "debug.ui.persona_allocation"
msgstr "Persona"

msgid "opening.allocation.title"
msgstr "What kind of nightwalker are you?"

msgid "opening.allocation.remaining"
msgstr "Points remaining: %d"

msgid "opening.allocation.enter"
msgstr "Enter the Atrium"

msgid "opening.allocation.persona.light.body"
msgstr "Excels at [color=#%s]reason and investigation[/color].\nNight makes my mind clearer."

msgid "opening.allocation.persona.tear.body"
msgstr "Excels at [color=#%s]empathy and compassion[/color].\nNight reminds me of sorrowful things."

msgid "opening.allocation.persona.dream.body"
msgstr "Excels at [color=#%s]fantasy and inspiration[/color].\nNight leaves my inspiration nowhere to hide."

msgid "opening.allocation.persona.sleep.body"
msgstr "Excels at [color=#%s]comfort and affinity[/color].\nMay I sleep well tonight, tonight."

msgid "opening.rules.0.welcome"
msgstr "Welcome to the Next Millennium Mall."

msgid "opening.rules.0.intro"
msgstr "To ensure a pleasant shopping experience, please observe the following rules:"

msgid "opening.rules.1"
msgstr "Rule 1: If you hear the merchandise whispering, please remain calm. They will return to silence shortly."

msgid "opening.rules.2.1"
msgstr "Rule 2: After checkout, please replace your head with your purchased merchandise."

msgid "opening.rules.2.2"
msgstr "If you are unwilling to do so, you must at least cover your head with a shopping bag."

msgid "opening.rules.3.1"
msgstr "Rule 3: Fireworks are strictly prohibited within the mall."

msgid "opening.rules.3.2"
msgstr "If you see fireworks, immediately seek assistance from a patrolling scanner."

msgid "opening.rules.4"
msgstr "Rule 4: When the broadcast advises you to \"run,\" you must flee immediately."

msgid "opening.rules.5.1"
msgstr "Rule 5: All clocks in the mall are stopped at 23:59:59."

msgid "opening.rules.5.2"
msgstr "However, should you observe a clock running, please jump and cheer loudly until we are able to find you."

msgid "opening.rules.6.1"
msgstr "Rule 6: There are still stores operating in the atrium. They are highly likely to be safe."

msgid "opening.rules.6.2"
msgstr "If you treat the shopkeepers kindly, they will treat you kindly in return."

msgid "opening.rules.6.3"
msgstr "— With the exception of one store."

msgid "title.ui.start_game"
msgstr "Start Game"
